Hello! I'm currently trying to strain-type my experimentally-obtained MLGs (diploid, microsatellite), but I'd like to use a database of strains to compare my experimental MLGs to. Previously, I have used the 'mlg.filter' function to strain-type MLGs using Bruvo's distance, but I've never used the function to strain-type against a database. I'm hoping I can be pointed in the right direction for this. I did glance over the previous topics in this group but couldn't find what I'm looking for, so apologies if this has been answered elsewhere! Thank you very much!

